# Singly Linked List (SLL) - 8 Interview Points

1. Definition: Chain of nodes, each has `data + next` pointer, unidirectional.
2. Head: First node reference           3. Tail: Last node, `next=None` (end marker).
4. Non-contiguous: Nodes anywhere in memory, linked by pointers.
5. O(1) insert/delete at head/tail (if tail ptr exists).
6. O(n) access by index (must traverse from head).
7. Dynamic size: Grow/shrink without reallocation.
8. Use cases: Stack/queue impl, undo history, sparse arrays.


